  "changes": [
    "Separate decoder identity from the four frozen capture producer identities. Fixed source/ETL hashes and each original producer name/size/hash are checked before and after reading.",
    "Read every ETL event and account for all buffers/loss counters. Retain every heap-provider record, including foreign PIDs and unrecognized opcodes/versions, without relabeling.",
    "Retain complete80-byte event headers, buffer context, payloads and extended-data items for every heap record. Record timestamps are ProcessTrace FILETIME values; no manual conversion/tolerance is used.",
    "Call native TDH for each unique schema and retain full TRACE_EVENT_INFO bytes. Read bounded actual top-level TDH property bytes. Missing/complex/unavailable metadata is explicitly retained rather than interpreted using a guessed layout.",
    "Never invoke the v1 version-zero heap parser or accept version2 on size alone. No alloc/free/live-negative/caller-stack capability flag becomes true in this stage."
  ],
  "bounds": {
    "ETL_bytes": 262144,
    "max_decode_seconds": 30,
